    {
      "id": "imperatif-conseils",
      "title": "L'impératif pour donner des conseils",
      "minutes": 10,
      "lede": "The imperative gives orders, instructions and advice. It has an affirmative and a negative form, and pronominal verbs have special rules.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "title": "Forme affirmative et négative",
          "headers": [
            "Forme",
            "Exemple"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "affirmative",
              "Buvez de l'eau."
            ],
            [
              "négative",
              "Ne mangez pas trop de sucre."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "title": "L'impératif des verbes pronominaux",
          "headers": [
            "Forme",
            "Exemple"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "affirmative",
              "Couche-toi tôt ! · Couchez-vous tôt !"
            ],
            [
              "négative",
              "Ne te couche pas tard ! · Ne vous couchez pas tard !"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Gotchas",
          "text": "- Three forms only: tu, nous, vous. They are the present tense without the subject: tu prends → Prends ! nous mangeons → Mangeons ! vous buvez → Buvez !\n- -er verbs lose the s in the tu form: Tu regardes → Regarde ! Tu manges → Mange ! (Only for -er verbs and aller: Va !)\n- Negative: ne (n') + verb + pas: Ne mangez pas trop de sucre. Ne vous couchez pas tard. (not “ne pas mangez”)\n- Pronominal verbs: in the affirmative, the pronoun goes after the verb with a hyphen, and te becomes toi: Couche-toi ! Assieds-toi ! Asseyez-vous ! In the negative, it stays before the verb: Ne te couche pas !\n- Don't confuse the imperative with the infinitive of general instructions (Leçon 20: Couper les tomates). Both give instructions: the imperative speaks to someone directly (Coupez!), the infinitive is impersonal (Couper).\n- Several commands in a row are linked by et or just a comma: Asseyez-vous et buvez de l'eau.\n- Imperative of être and avoir are irregular: sois / soyez, aie / ayez (Sois gentil ! N'ayez pas peur !): you will meet them later."
        },
